From 8c5101a3f5ca39703dc7176b1ed01b4685bb9ecd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Sat, 15 Aug 2026 10:46:55 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [DOSKUTSU] patch 0305 -- let the engine decomposition emit on
 the fixed path

0304 restored the COARSE engine bucket during GM_NORMAL gameplay. The
FINE decomposition stayed dark for the same reason one level down: the
`[engine-tick-stat]` block is gated on g_eng_residual_idx > 0, and the
residual is pushed exclusively inside Game::tick, which the
fixed-timestep GM_NORMAL path never calls.

The data was already there. The sub-bucket timers (ClearScreenTimer,
TscInterpTimer, ModeTickStateTimer, ModeTickRenderTimer,
DebugOverlayTimer) all run inside tick_state / tick_render_submit and
fill their arrays correctly throughout gameplay -- only the gate was
shut. Witnessed on the 0304 QA-reel run: 3 emits across 185 blocks.

Emit when ANY sub-bucket has samples. Measured on the same reel after:
121 emits across 121 blocks, all seven phases present, with
mode_tick_render at ~2.7 ms/flip the dominant sub-bucket and
clear_screen ~0.06, mode_tick_state ~0.28.

The residual is deliberately NOT synthesized for the fixed path. It is
defined as un-bracketed time inside ONE Game::tick body, and that path
has no such body -- tick_state runs 0..N times per displayed frame
against tick_render_submit's once. Inventing a number under the existing
label would make engine_tick_residual mean two different things
depending on which path produced the line; it prints n=0 instead, which
is honest, and the line says so itself.

Second hunk, a defect this widening exposes rather than introduces: the
residual line was emitted WITHOUT the n>0 guard every sibling phase has.
That was safe only while the old gate guaranteed a non-empty array.
Reached with n=0 it ran _compute_flip_phase_stats over uninitialized
storage and printed min/med 515404.69 ms with p95 4294.99 -- 2^32/1e6,
the giveaway. Guarded to match its siblings. A stale huge number sitting
in a log beside real per-phase timings is exactly what gets quoted at
face value later.

Why this matters before the next hardware trip: without it a real-HW
FINE_INSTR=1 cell returns the engine bucket TOTAL but not its
breakdown -- half the answer for a full operator trip, and the breakdown
is the half that says where the engine time actually goes.

Both hunks are inside the existing FINE_INSTR-gated block, so the
default binary is unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Code <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 src/graphics/Renderer.cpp | 55 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---
 1 file changed, 51 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
index b58da4b3..2d10499f 100644
--- a/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
+++ b/src/graphics/Renderer.cpp
@@ -2673,7 +2673,37 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
   // Output prefix `engine-tick-stat` distinct from W20A's `flip-stat`
   // and the parked W20B-flip-body's `flip-fine-stat` so grep tooling
   // can separate the three layers without ambiguity.
-  if (_abl_fine_instr() && NXE::Diag::g_eng_residual_idx > 0)
+  // DOS-PORT (patch 0305): emit when ANY sub-bucket has samples, not only
+  // when the residual does. The residual is pushed exclusively inside
+  // Game::tick (game.cpp), which the FIXED-TIMESTEP GM_NORMAL path never
+  // calls -- so gating the whole block on it kept the engine decomposition
+  // dark during the gameplay every measured cell runs, one level below the
+  // coarse-bucket blindness 0304 fixed. Witnessed on the 0304 QA-reel run:
+  // 3 emits across 185 blocks, while the sub-bucket timers inside
+  // tick_state / tick_render_submit were filling their arrays correctly the
+  // whole time. The data was there; only the gate was shut.
+  //
+  // The residual is deliberately NOT synthesized for the fixed path. It is
+  // defined as un-bracketed time inside ONE Game::tick body, and the fixed
+  // path has no such body -- tick_state runs 0..N times per displayed frame
+  // against tick_render_submit's once. Manufacturing a number under the
+  // existing label would make `engine_tick_residual` mean two different
+  // things depending on which path produced the line, which is exactly the
+  // mixed-provenance trap that has already cost this campaign one retracted
+  // result. It prints n=0 there instead, which is honest: on the fixed path
+  // the residual is genuinely undefined, and its own line says so.
+  //
+  // Reads the sub-bucket idxes rather than re-deriving anything. They are
+  // reset unconditionally below (outside this guard), so a block that does
+  // not emit still clears -- no stale accumulation either way.
+  if (_abl_fine_instr()
+      && (NXE::Diag::g_eng_residual_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_clear_screen_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_tsc_interp_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_mode_tick_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_mode_tick_state_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_mode_tick_render_idx > 0
+          || NXE::Diag::g_eng_debug_overlay_idx > 0))
   {
     using NXE::Diag::g_eng_clear_screen_samples;
     using NXE::Diag::g_eng_tsc_interp_samples;
@@ -2762,9 +2792,26 @@ void _maybe_flush_phase_timing_audit()
     {
       LOG_INFO("[engine-tick-stat n=0 phase=debug_overlay         min=0.00 med=0.00 mean=0.00 p95=0.00 max=0.00 ms]");
     }
-    _compute_flip_phase_stats(g_eng_residual_samples, n_res, st_res);
-    LOG_INFO("[engine-tick-stat n={} phase=engine_tick_residual  min={:.2f} med={:.2f} mean={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} ms]",
-             n_res, st_res.min_ms, st_res.med_ms, st_res.mean_ms, st_res.p95_ms, st_res.max_ms);
+    // DOS-PORT (patch 0305): n>0 guard, matching every sibling phase above.
+    // This line was previously unguarded, which was safe only because the
+    // old emit condition (residual_idx > 0) meant it could never be reached
+    // with an empty array. Widening that condition breaks the assumption:
+    // on the fixed-timestep path the residual is legitimately empty, and
+    // _compute_flip_phase_stats over n=0 read uninitialized storage and
+    // printed garbage -- observed as min/med 515404.69 ms and p95 4294.99
+    // (that is 2^32/1e6, the giveaway). A stale huge number sitting in a
+    // log next to real per-phase timings is precisely what gets quoted at
+    // face value later, so it must not be emitted at all.
+    if (n_res > 0)
+    {
+      _compute_flip_phase_stats(g_eng_residual_samples, n_res, st_res);
+      LOG_INFO("[engine-tick-stat n={} phase=engine_tick_residual  min={:.2f} med={:.2f} mean={:.2f} p95={:.2f} max={:.2f} ms]",
+               n_res, st_res.min_ms, st_res.med_ms, st_res.mean_ms, st_res.p95_ms, st_res.max_ms);
+    }
+    else
+    {
+      LOG_INFO("[engine-tick-stat n=0 phase=engine_tick_residual  min=0.00 med=0.00 mean=0.00 p95=0.00 max=0.00 ms]");
+    }
   }
   // Reset engine-tick sample arrays + idxes regardless of FINE_INSTR
   // state -- keeps storage cleanly zeroed for the next block.
-- 
